{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/generation"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outDegree(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outEdges(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/successors(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/vertexIndex(checked:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs on it, including those that need","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge storage.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches instead: Traversal’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ShortestPaths’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states over a finite set, number them and use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A grid is numbered row-major.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The closure","anchor":"The-closure","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":", such as an array or a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list. A specialized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call it once each, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" once per vertex."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex. This is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not checked, and a closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm. Each target is checked to be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and yields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them by count. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy.filter"},{"type":"text","text":" calls its predicate per element and carries the unfiltered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator’s state, which costs more per edge."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Positions","anchor":"Positions","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":", which holds its source, its rank in the source’s row, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"type":"text","text":", which is unique even among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges and self-loops. Because the position carries the target, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a weight closure reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge indices."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Attached values","anchor":"Attached-values","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because ","type":"text"},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a dense offset only after every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier row is counted. Keep vertex values in an array of ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indexed by vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compute edge values from the position (","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", because a closure has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored."}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L48","fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/OutEdges":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OutEdges"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The positions of the edges leaving one vertex, in row order: ranks 0, 1, …, each with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"target, checked to be a vertex as it is read."}],"title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.OutEdges","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/impli